WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:03.840
A long, long time ago.

00:04.060 --> 00:06.740
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:07.630 --> 00:12.380
Nadja, guided by destiny, arrived in France.

00:16.580 --> 00:17.880
NAAJA

00:16.580 --> 00:17.880
Nadja,

00:18.000 --> 00:20.540
With your eyes

00:18.000 --> 00:20.540
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
Nadja,

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
NAAJA

00:21.790 --> 00:24.050
What do you see?

00:21.790 --> 00:24.050
Nani ga mieru

00:24.080 --> 00:26.960
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:24.090 --> 00:26.970
Shining in the far distance,

00:26.980 --> 00:29.360
The door to the future,

00:26.980 --> 00:29.360
Mirai no tobira

00:30.240 --> 00:33.720
That's what I'm searching for

00:30.240 --> 00:33.720
Sagashite iru

00:33.720 --> 00:40.940
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:41.640 --> 00:45.160
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:41.640 --> 00:45.160
Minna egao de aetara

00:45.240 --> 00:48.490
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:45.240 --> 00:48.490
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:48.520 --> 00:51.730
It could be so much more fun

00:48.520 --> 00:51.730
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:51.790 --> 00:55.210
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:51.790 --> 00:55.210
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:55.570 --> 00:58.870
I can't see the end of the journey

00:55.570 --> 00:58.870
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:58.990 --> 01:02.320
God is the only one who could possibly know

00:58.990 --> 01:02.320
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:02.510 --> 01:06.100
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:02.510 --> 01:06.100
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:06.140 --> 01:08.260
I will go waving

01:06.140 --> 01:08.260
Te wo furinagara

01:08.340 --> 01:15.000
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:08.340 --> 01:15.000
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.070 --> 01:17.780
But I won't look back

01:15.070 --> 01:17.780
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.110 --> 01:23.070
Until the day my dream comes true

01:18.110 --> 01:23.070
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:23.360 --> 01:26.780
Nadja, Your smile

01:23.360 --> 01:26.780
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:26.840 --> 01:30.180
Nadja, gives me courage

01:26.840 --> 01:30.180
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:30.250 --> 01:33.170
Under the blue sky,

01:30.250 --> 01:33.170
Aoi sora no shita de

01:33.270 --> 01:36.100
I will find the place

01:33.270 --> 01:36.100
Ashita no yukue

01:36.430 --> 01:40.340
where my future lies

01:36.430 --> 01:40.340
Mitsukeru kara

01:46.050 --> 01:50.480
I hope that Sylvie and Raphael
find happiness one day.

01:51.110 --> 01:53.490
And...as for me...

01:55.110 --> 01:56.110
Francis...

01:56.740 --> 01:58.360
The star-eyed knight...

01:59.030 --> 02:01.490
I'm sure...we'll meet again, right...

02:03.160 --> 02:05.200
Nadja, can you lend me a hand?

02:06.040 --> 02:07.040
Yes!

02:13.480 --> 02:18.320
The Troubled Genius Pianist!

02:19.300 --> 02:20.590
Madame Moreau?

02:20.600 --> 02:24.600
Hmmm, it's Baron Moreau's
wife, Lady Mireille.

02:26.030 --> 02:30.280
With that said , she's not a typical
noblewoman. However...

02:30.530 --> 02:32.440
Ah, here it is, here it is.

02:35.100 --> 02:36.720
What a splendid mansion!

02:39.320 --> 02:41.910
My, this is gorgeous!

02:42.180 --> 02:45.230
Your hats are always works of art!

02:47.120 --> 02:50.920
Say, Anna, you still haven't decided
to open up a shop in Paris?

02:51.170 --> 02:52.880
Thank you for your praise,

02:53.070 --> 02:56.570
but my current life as a
traveler suits me well.

02:56.720 --> 02:59.300
I give up. You're not ambitious at all.

02:59.600 --> 03:03.270
Oh yes, Nadja, your dance sure is splendid.

03:04.720 --> 03:07.180
I secretly went to see your performance.

03:07.420 --> 03:10.960
If you wish to study formally,
come to me anytime.

03:11.000 --> 03:12.540
Eh? Umm...

03:13.820 --> 03:17.110
Madame Moreau assists the
youths that have talent...

03:17.150 --> 03:19.440
...in various different ways.

03:20.890 --> 03:22.100
Is that right?

03:22.700 --> 03:24.660
It's nothing special.

03:24.830 --> 03:27.120
So that young artists can gather...

03:27.420 --> 03:29.210
I host a salon, that's all.

03:29.590 --> 03:30.500
Salon?

03:42.700 --> 03:43.950
This is the salon?

03:44.760 --> 03:48.850
People who wish to pursue the arts,
are free to spend their time here.

03:49.500 --> 03:51.510
You are also welcome anytime.

03:52.000 --> 03:53.210
Ah, yes!

04:28.430 --> 04:31.270
Splendid...such a gentle sound.

04:31.310 --> 04:33.270
He is John Whittard.

04:33.460 --> 04:35.460
A young genius composer.

04:35.820 --> 04:37.240
A genius composer?

04:51.630 --> 04:54.880
Wow!! If it isn't my Little Rosebud!

04:56.480 --> 04:58.240
Leonardo and Thierry!

05:00.740 --> 05:03.490
To meet in a place like this! It must be fate.

05:04.030 --> 05:04.990
You've made me happy.

05:07.300 --> 05:08.720
This guy doesn't know when to stop.

05:10.730 --> 05:12.190
Ah? I see!

05:12.500 --> 05:15.040
Thierry's here because you're
a designer, aren't you?

05:15.320 --> 05:15.780
Yup.

05:16.320 --> 05:17.490
I just tagged along.

05:17.840 --> 05:20.470
Because this is a lovely "flower garden."

05:21.770 --> 05:25.140
I never thought you two would
be acquainted with Nadja.

05:27.030 --> 05:30.360
It's because "all the beautiful things
in the world are mine."

05:30.680 --> 05:32.220
Of course, Mireille...

05:32.360 --> 05:33.440
...you are as well.

05:35.380 --> 05:36.940
Oh my...

05:38.780 --> 05:39.860
Say Thierry...

05:40.130 --> 05:42.380
While I have a chat with Anna...

05:42.570 --> 05:45.520
...can you protect Nadja
from Leonardo's fangs?

05:45.600 --> 05:46.860
"Fangs" you say?!

05:46.900 --> 05:48.090
Of course I will.

05:48.120 --> 05:49.920
Well Nadja, I'll see you later.

05:50.190 --> 05:51.350
Ah, yes Ma'am!

05:52.920 --> 05:56.130
Nadja, everyone's taking me the wrong way!

05:58.990 --> 06:00.650
You're being noisy over there!

06:00.860 --> 06:03.520
This is not a place to be chatting with girls!

06:03.990 --> 06:06.910
The salon is a place to enjoy
social interaction.

06:07.390 --> 06:10.140
That's the problem with
straight-laced people.

06:10.310 --> 06:11.310
What?!

06:11.830 --> 06:14.670
Uh, I'm sorry we were being a nuisance.

06:15.030 --> 06:16.280
Who the heck are you?

06:17.690 --> 06:20.380
I'm...Nadja Applefield.

06:20.530 --> 06:23.110
I dance for the Dandelion Troupe.

06:23.620 --> 06:26.950
Dande-... Is that the name of a theater?

06:27.240 --> 06:29.450
No, it's a troupe of traveling performers.

06:29.890 --> 06:30.560
Huh!

06:31.540 --> 06:32.880
Traveling performers, huh?

06:33.190 --> 06:34.560
The way you say that isn't...

06:34.830 --> 06:35.410
Hey!

06:35.440 --> 06:37.980
This is no good! I can't concentrate here!

06:43.090 --> 06:44.840
I wonder if we did something wrong...

06:44.940 --> 06:45.980
Forget it.

06:46.240 --> 06:48.330
He may be a genius at composing, but...

06:48.840 --> 06:50.580
...he's hopeless at melding with others.

06:51.140 --> 06:52.230
I see...

06:52.790 --> 06:55.370
After winning the composition
concours in England...

06:52.800 --> 06:55.360
[concours = french for competition]

06:55.490 --> 06:57.750
...he came to Paris by himself,
or so I've heard.

06:57.880 --> 06:58.800
England?!

06:59.300 --> 07:01.090
I come from England as well!

07:01.450 --> 07:03.320
Oh, I see.

07:03.610 --> 07:08.570
It's rumored that John is certain to be the winner
of the next concours in Paris as well.

07:08.950 --> 07:10.160
Really?

07:10.660 --> 07:13.910
But, it was mean of him to talk that way
about traveling performers, wasn't it?

07:18.520 --> 07:19.520
Nadja!

07:19.640 --> 07:22.060
Could you go and buy some
bread for lunch please?

07:22.150 --> 07:23.030
Yes!

07:26.050 --> 07:26.890
I'll go too!

07:28.560 --> 07:30.100
Okay! Let's go! Let's go!

07:49.320 --> 07:50.420
What is it?

07:50.780 --> 07:53.740
Well. French bread is delicious, but...

07:54.120 --> 07:58.380
Sometimes it would be nice to have rice, I think.

07:58.480 --> 07:59.540
Rice?

08:00.710 --> 08:02.420
I see, you don't know what that is?

08:02.820 --> 08:04.110
Rice is a kind of grain.

08:04.300 --> 08:05.660
It's the Japanese staple.

08:05.840 --> 08:06.920
Ohh!

08:07.010 --> 08:09.050
I understand your sentiments, Kennosuke.

08:09.490 --> 08:11.330
I think about it once in a while too...

08:11.560 --> 08:16.390
French bread is good, but it would be nice to
have a soft English sandwich too, I think.

08:16.480 --> 08:17.640
I see!

08:19.740 --> 08:21.420
What is it, Rita?

08:24.920 --> 08:26.260
H-Hold it!

08:28.260 --> 08:30.340
No, don't commit suicide!

08:33.500 --> 08:35.370
Don't waste your life!

08:35.600 --> 08:38.860
Y-You insult me! Who's
trying to kill himself?

08:42.990 --> 08:45.030
You're yesterday's...!

08:46.390 --> 08:47.720
Do you...know him?

08:48.010 --> 08:50.720
Mr. Genius was trying to
commit suicide? Why...

08:50.800 --> 08:52.000
I wasn't trying to commit suicide.

08:52.140 --> 08:54.270
I was just trying to get a better
look at the Seine River!

08:56.000 --> 08:56.870
Don't touch it!

08:59.170 --> 09:02.250
Inside are very important music
sheets for the concours!

09:02.540 --> 09:04.210
Then don't drop it!

09:04.580 --> 09:07.840
Scaring a girl. As a samurai
I won't allow that!

09:08.060 --> 09:08.810
Samurai?

09:09.220 --> 09:10.180
What the heck is that?

09:14.870 --> 09:15.450
Cats!

09:18.440 --> 09:20.860
If I touch cats, I...

09:22.150 --> 09:23.380
Get a hold of yourself!!

09:24.170 --> 09:25.840
These aren't cats...

09:47.430 --> 09:50.180
That was the world's smallest
lion tamer, Lady Rita...

09:50.550 --> 09:53.800
...and her twin lions, Cream and Chocolat!

09:55.370 --> 09:58.160
Lions? So they weren't cats?

09:58.460 --> 10:00.080
Now next up, the one you've
been waiting for.

10:00.350 --> 10:04.230
Descending onto Paris, the miraculous
dancing princess, Lady Nadja!

10:04.500 --> 10:05.340
Nadja?!

10:15.520 --> 10:17.940
She dances with such joy...that girl...

11:20.840 --> 11:22.100
Thank you very much!

11:22.490 --> 11:23.500
Thank you very much!

11:24.010 --> 11:26.100
Your Dandelion Troupe's...

11:26.140 --> 11:29.890
...performances have finished for the day.

11:37.260 --> 11:38.720
It was fun, wasn't it?

11:39.590 --> 11:42.220
Were you pleased with our performance?

11:42.720 --> 11:44.320
Who's pleased?

11:45.560 --> 11:49.060
The acts of traveling performers isn't art.

11:49.520 --> 11:50.690
It's just playing around.

11:50.830 --> 11:52.460
W-What did you say?!

12:20.780 --> 12:22.440
Playing around you say...?!

12:22.530 --> 12:24.160
Are you a violinist?

12:24.890 --> 12:26.800
With that self taught form of yours,

12:26.830 --> 12:29.200
you'd be eliminated at a concours, right from the start.

12:29.220 --> 12:30.180
What?!

12:30.250 --> 12:31.620
Now, now, now.

12:32.540 --> 12:34.670
You compose music, right?

12:35.000 --> 12:37.000
The concours must be difficult, huh?

12:37.210 --> 12:38.710
It's very competitive, right?

12:40.380 --> 12:44.680
Just as you said, it's true that
what we do isn't art.

12:44.930 --> 12:48.470
To make enough money to live,
we sell our performance.

12:50.100 --> 12:50.930
But still...

12:51.430 --> 12:53.730
...it's much harder than you might think.

12:54.140 --> 12:57.270
The judges at a concours will
listen until you finish, but...

12:57.310 --> 12:59.270
...when it comes to our customers...

12:59.570 --> 13:02.400
If they feel bored they just go home.

13:02.440 --> 13:05.910
But after watching our performance,
some people say, "That was fun!"

13:05.950 --> 13:08.280
...or "It cheered me up!"

13:08.830 --> 13:11.620
It's not art, but we are doing
something useful.

13:12.080 --> 13:14.250
And while we live on the road...

13:14.290 --> 13:16.500
...there are many wonderful encounters.

13:16.670 --> 13:19.420
That's why we do our best.

13:20.630 --> 13:21.710
Exactly.

13:21.930 --> 13:22.680
Yup.

13:26.110 --> 13:28.660
I don't have the time for
such a stupid discussion.

13:28.930 --> 13:30.890
You're still saying the same thing?

13:30.930 --> 13:33.180
If you keep talking so rudely like that...

13:33.270 --> 13:34.140
Take this!

13:38.510 --> 13:39.840
There's nothing written...

13:41.400 --> 13:45.070
What the heck!? You were so snotty
about it being your concours entry!

13:45.490 --> 13:49.620
Ah! The truth of the matter
is, you can't compose squat!

13:49.770 --> 13:50.640
Shut up!

13:52.400 --> 13:53.250
John!

13:54.370 --> 13:55.740
Wait up!

13:56.040 --> 13:57.710
Hold it, Kennosuke.

13:58.720 --> 14:00.460
Leave it to Nadja, all right?

14:00.500 --> 14:01.200
What?

14:01.460 --> 14:04.760
Well now. It's almost time for tea, isn't it?

14:38.830 --> 14:40.330
I'm back to where I started?

14:41.960 --> 14:43.250
I can't do this anymore!

14:52.330 --> 14:53.500
You sure don't give up...

14:53.680 --> 14:54.390
Eh?

14:54.550 --> 14:56.220
You...think so?

14:56.240 --> 14:57.980
And you're too fast for me.

14:58.060 --> 15:00.770
I became fast by running over English hills.

15:00.970 --> 15:03.020
So you grew up in England too?

15:03.060 --> 15:03.660
Yes!

15:03.900 --> 15:04.940
I see.

15:06.740 --> 15:10.030
But, you have all your friends with you.

15:10.490 --> 15:15.410
We may be both English, but you're completely
different from me, who came to Paris alone.

15:15.910 --> 15:17.080
Umm...

15:18.580 --> 15:21.670
I only joined the Dandelion Troupe...

15:21.880 --> 15:23.170
...this spring.

15:24.800 --> 15:27.340
I grew up in an orphanage in England.

15:27.670 --> 15:29.340
I have my reasons, but I had to leave...

15:30.090 --> 15:32.340
Then when I was all alone and
wondering what to do...

15:32.470 --> 15:34.260
...the troupe came to my rescue.

15:35.010 --> 15:36.200
This spring...

15:40.140 --> 15:41.480
You're something else.

15:44.360 --> 15:46.610
Why are you so quick to make friends?

15:48.530 --> 15:50.650
With Thierry and Leonardo, as well...

15:50.990 --> 15:53.200
...you've probably only known them for a couple of months, right?

15:53.700 --> 15:55.620
I met them last week.

15:56.870 --> 16:00.290
And, I met Madame Moreau
for the first time yesterday.

16:02.210 --> 16:03.710
Are you all right?

16:04.250 --> 16:06.340
It's just as I thought, you really are something else.

16:07.000 --> 16:08.920
Why am I so hopeless?

16:09.300 --> 16:12.010
All this time, I couldn't get close to anyone.

16:12.510 --> 16:15.260
I was so busy worrying about it, that I was unable to compose.

16:15.930 --> 16:20.350
If you guys didn't stop me, I'd be at the bottom of the Seine River by now.

16:25.230 --> 16:26.270
Oh yes!

16:26.610 --> 16:28.440
Can you please wait here a moment?

16:29.610 --> 16:30.990
Granny!

16:31.240 --> 16:32.780
It's time for tea!

16:37.450 --> 16:38.580
Thank you!

16:38.620 --> 16:40.250
Don't mention it, don't mention it.

16:42.870 --> 16:44.000
Could it be...?

16:44.380 --> 16:45.400
It's tea.

16:45.710 --> 16:48.710
From England. Of course it's milk tea.

16:52.950 --> 16:54.380
Here you are.

16:58.850 --> 17:00.060
It has a nice scent.

17:02.350 --> 17:04.520
This flavour is so relaxing.

17:04.620 --> 17:05.700
Isn't it?

17:08.150 --> 17:10.570
French bread and cafe au lait are good and all...

17:10.730 --> 17:16.120
...but when I'm a little tired, I start to miss English sandwiches and tea.

17:16.240 --> 17:16.870
Yup.

17:17.370 --> 17:20.700
I couldn't bring the bread, but
I brought plenty of tea.

17:21.370 --> 17:22.250
I see now.

17:32.460 --> 17:34.970
I've been drinking cafe au lait all this time.

17:35.220 --> 17:35.840
Eh?

17:36.690 --> 17:38.950
I thought, "I have to get
used to France quickly."

17:39.850 --> 17:43.020
I was raised to believe that I was a "genius" in England.

17:43.520 --> 17:45.390
I was pretty confident, but...

17:46.350 --> 17:50.070
...when I came to Paris and found plenty of talented people... I was shocked.

17:50.560 --> 17:53.780
Afraid of being thought of as a bumpkin, I tried to act important.

17:54.570 --> 17:57.280
By the time I realized what I was
doing, the damage was done.

18:03.770 --> 18:04.730
Thanks.

18:06.540 --> 18:07.710
There was someone before...

18:08.420 --> 18:09.750
...who came and offered me tea.

18:11.170 --> 18:13.590
In England, when I entered a public school...

18:13.960 --> 18:17.130
...just like now, when I couldn't
make any friends....

18:17.430 --> 18:20.390
...a dorm mate of mine came
and offered me tea.

18:21.140 --> 18:24.180
He said, "It's great that you always
play like you're having fun."

18:27.870 --> 18:30.080
Someone said the same thing
to me the other day.

18:30.640 --> 18:32.780
He said I was having fun dancing.

18:39.490 --> 18:41.040
I thought so a while ago too.

18:41.490 --> 18:43.160
You dance with such joy.

18:43.660 --> 18:45.620
Same with the rest of the
troupe with their acts.

18:45.950 --> 18:47.660
I felt envious.

18:48.210 --> 18:50.250
But, I'm not used to being honest.

18:50.570 --> 18:52.280
I heard you playing on the piano yesterday.

18:52.460 --> 18:54.460
It was a really gentle sound.

18:56.130 --> 18:59.430
I'm sure it's because you love the piano and music, John!

18:59.930 --> 19:03.430
I think that the things you love are always fun.

19:03.680 --> 19:05.970
Things you love are always fun, huh?

19:07.060 --> 19:08.190
Now that you mention it...

19:10.650 --> 19:12.560
...the first time I touched a piano...

19:12.900 --> 19:15.690
I had fun striking the keys
and making sound.

19:16.070 --> 19:19.990
I didn't want to leave the piano, and I made trouble for my mother.

19:21.660 --> 19:23.580
When I first started studying with a teacher...

19:23.910 --> 19:25.240
I felt so proud.

19:27.540 --> 19:30.420
I became tired of the practice pieces,
and wrote my own composition.

19:30.830 --> 19:33.380
I thought she would be angry,
but she praised me...

19:33.750 --> 19:35.000
I was so happy.

19:39.260 --> 19:42.890
Back then, I was happy as long
as I could play the piano.

19:44.050 --> 19:44.930
Forever...

19:45.640 --> 19:47.620
I wanted to keep playing forever.

19:52.990 --> 19:55.620
I remember now! The reason
why I detest cats!

19:56.190 --> 19:58.400
Long ago, I was scratched badly by a cat.

19:58.740 --> 20:00.950
I couldn't play the piano
for a while, and I cried.

20:03.280 --> 20:05.990
That's why I wouldn't go near cats again.

20:06.370 --> 20:07.740
I see.

20:08.250 --> 20:10.500
But Cream and Chocolat are lions though.

20:10.890 --> 20:11.680
Yeah...

20:12.580 --> 20:14.460
Ah, would you like another?

20:14.750 --> 20:15.590
I've had enough.

20:16.100 --> 20:17.100
Thanks for the drink.

20:19.150 --> 20:21.730
I want to play...the piano with joy!

20:22.260 --> 20:24.640
And I want to put those feelings
into my composition.

20:25.600 --> 20:26.160
John!

20:26.640 --> 20:27.600
Thanks Nadja!

20:28.140 --> 20:29.640
Please give my regards to the
Master and the others.

20:51.050 --> 20:52.310
My, John?

20:52.500 --> 20:54.210
You seem lively today.

20:54.250 --> 20:55.460
Yes, I'm feeling great.

20:59.630 --> 21:00.880
Hey, John.

21:03.970 --> 21:05.010
Francis!

21:05.840 --> 21:07.100
I just arrived a while ago.

21:07.390 --> 21:09.350
I'm here for a charity event.

21:09.520 --> 21:11.810
Speak of the devil...

21:11.980 --> 21:15.520
I was just talking about you to a girl.

21:15.560 --> 21:18.570
Remember? About how you
offered me tea in the dorm.

21:18.630 --> 21:19.380
